LOCATION:ESKENAZI SCHOOL OF ART\, ARCHITECTURE + DESIGN MIES VAN DER ROHE
  BUILDING
GEO:39.169141;-86.516625
SUMMARY:Latine Art Panel
DESCRIPTION:Being held at the Mies van der Rohe Building on the IU Bloomi
 ngton campus\, the conversation will explore themes of identity\, belongi
 ng\, representation\, and the power of collective creativity to strengthe
 n communities and foster connection.  &#160\;Exhibition: September 15–1
 8\, 11am–5 pm\, FAR Center\, 505 W Fourth Street  A joint production of
  the FAR Center for Contemporary Arts\, IU's Eskenazi School\, and IU's L
 a Casa/Latino Cultural Center\, the discussion will feature artists parti
 cipating in the exhibition FUERZA—the 2026 Hispanic Heritage theme—be
 ing held at the FAR Center September 15–18. The exhibition features wor
 k across two- and three-dimensional media created by Hispanic-identifying
  Indiana residents or students.  &#160\;Closing reception and artist mark
 et: September 18\, 5–9:30 pm\, FAR Center\, 505 W Fourth Street  A rece
 ption on September 18 at the FAR Center will feature an artist market whe
 re exhibiting artists will have an opportunity to sell work\, along with 
 live music and dancing from 8–9:30 pm with the Salsoteca band led by Se
 rgio Ospina Romero. Food will be provided for sale by Pilis Party Taco an
 d Midnight Mariposa Bakery.  Visit here for more information about FUERZA
 :https://events.thefar.org/events/event/122905 (https://events.thefar.org
 /events/event/122905)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="p1">  Being held at the Mies van d
 er Rohe Building on the IU Bloomington campus\, the conversation will exp
 lore themes of identity\, belonging\, representation\, and the power of c
 ollective creativity to strengthen communities and foster connection.</p>
 <p class="p1">  &#160\;</p><p class="p1"><strong>Exhibition:</strong> Sep
 tember 15–18\, 11am–5 pm\, FAR Center\, 505 W Fourth Street</p><p cla
 ss="p1">  A joint production of the FAR Center for Contemporary Arts\, IU
 's Eskenazi School\, and IU's La Casa/Latino Cultural Center\, the discus
 sion will feature artists participating in the exhibition FUERZA—the 20
 26 Hispanic Heritage theme—being held at the FAR Center September 15–
 18. The exhibition features work across two- and three-dimensional media 
 created by Hispanic-identifying Indiana residents or students.</p><p clas
 s="p1">  &#160\;</p><p class="p1"><strong>Closing reception and artist ma
 rket:</strong> September 18\, 5–9:30 pm\, FAR Center\, 505 W Fourth Str
 eet</p><p class="p1">  A reception on September 18 at the FAR Center will
  feature an artist market where exhibiting artists will have an opportuni
 ty to sell work\, along with live music and dancing from 8–9:30 pm with
  the Salsoteca band led by Sergio Ospina Romero. Food will be provided fo
 r sale by Pilis Party Taco and Midnight Mariposa Bakery.</p><p class="p1"
 >  Visit here for more information about FUERZA:<br /><a href="https://ev
 ents.thefar.org/events/event/122905">https://events.thefar.org/events/eve
 nt/122905</a></p>
