DTSTART:20260922T223000Z
DTEND:20260922T233000Z
LOCATION:La Casa/Latino Cultural Center
GEO:39.168732;-86.525021
SUMMARY:Latine Book Club: Alligator Tears
DESCRIPTION:Connecting through literature! Explore the world of Latine wr
 iters! Free books to first 10 IU students for each session who will atten
 d a gathering. Co-sponsored by Indiana University Student Government\, La
 tino Studies\, Center for Latin American &amp\; Caribbean Studies\, LGBTQ
 +CC\, and La Casa.Alligator Tears touches on themes of identity\, family\
 , and the precarities facing trans people\, especially those of color.&#1
 60\;  Edgar Gomez will be on campus on October 2nd at 11:30am at the IMU 
 Dogwood Room&#160\;for an event hosted by Latino Studies.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">
 Connecting through literature! Explore the world of Latine writers! Free 
 books to first 10 IU students for each session who will attend a gatherin
 g. Co-sponsored by Indiana University Student Government\, Latino Studies
 \, Center for Latin American &amp\; Caribbean Studies\, LGBTQ+CC\, and La
  Casa.</span></p><p><em>Alligator Tears</em> touches on themes of identit
 y\, family\, and the precarities facing trans people\, especially those o
 f color.&#160\;</p><p>  Edgar Gomez will be on campus on October 2nd at 1
 1:30am at the IMU <span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">Dogwood Room</
 span>&#160\;for an event hosted by Latino Studies.</p>
