BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU La Casa Latino Cultural Center
DTSTART:20261001T220000Z
DTEND:20261001T230000Z
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books
SUMMARY:Edgar Gómez book reading and signing
DESCRIPTION:Edgar Gomezis a queer NicaRican writer born and raised in Flo
 rida. He is the author of the memoirs High-Risk Homosexual (Soft Skull Pr
 ess\, 2022) and Alligator Tears (Crown\, 2025). For his writing he has re
 ceived the American Book Award\, a Stonewall Israel-Fishman Nonfiction Bo
 ok Honor Award\, a Florida Book Award\, and the Lambda Literary Award. 
  His work has been supported by The New York Foundation for the Arts\, Th
 e National Endowment for the Arts\, and The Black Mountain Institute. A g
 raduate of the University of California's MFA program\, Gomez has written
  for The LA Times\, Poets &amp\; Writers\, Lithub\, New York Magazine\, a
 nd beyond. He lives between New York and Puerto Rico.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong><span data-contrast="none">Edgar 
 Gomez</span></strong><span data-contrast="none">is a queer NicaRican writ
 er born and raised in Florida. He is the author of the memoirs High-Risk 
 Homosexual (Soft Skull Press\, 2022) and Alligator Tears (Crown\, 2025). 
 For his writing he has received the American Book Award\, a Stonewall Isr
 ael-Fishman Nonfiction Book Honor Award\, a Florida Book Award\, and the 
 Lambda Literary Award.  His work has been supported by The New York Fou
 ndation for the Arts\, The National Endowment for the Arts\, and The Blac
 k Mountain Institute. A graduate of the University of California's MFA pr
 ogram\, Gomez has written for The LA Times\, Poets &amp\; Writers\, Lithu
 b\, New York Magazine\, and beyond. He lives between New York and Puerto 
 Rico.</span><span data-ccp-props="{}"></span></p>
